 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Totally understandable. One way to switch off is with a routine change. After work, don't head straight to the desk. Sure, take your usual route and turn it into a walk instead. Lots of little parks here and there with play structures and green space. Another trick is a short warm up. Like five jumping jacks or a stretch before sitting in front of the screen. It tells your body it still moving. Okay, sure. We can stop at the shop to get milk though. It's been years since milk came in those big cartons. That's a good one too. Lots of people stop at the shop and then hit the sofa. A full body walk retrains your brain for off duty.",
